[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The renderer may know the shape of a view and never its content

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-VIEW-RENDERER-IS-CONTENT-BLIND
TITLE: The renderer may know the shape of a view and never its content
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
The renderer knows the wireline schema, the widget words and how to draw
each, the legend's colour vocabulary, and that a tree's children are tabs,
sections and cards in order. It knows no UID, no tag word, no node-type
name, no plan directory and no reading of one type through another. Every
word on the page comes from the payload: from a narrative's own fields, or
from a table a backed script computed from the export. A renderer edit that
is needed to show a new node, a new word or a new project violates this.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The operator's line: "the renderer can have opinions on the data it expects
to render ... the line is if the renderer needs any awareness of the
content." A renderer that knows content is a second, unreviewed copy of the
canon, which is what the one-off render's hand-written headlines were.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: DEC-VIEWS-ARE-REGENERABLE
  ROLE: Governed_By
